---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — Taxline"
  description="The terms governing your use of Taxline. Outputs require human review and are not tax, legal, or accounting advice — you remain responsible for your filings."
>
  <TopNav />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <p class="ds-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="ds-h1 mt-3">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint">Last updated: May 30, 2026</p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Acceptance</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of Taxline. By creating an account,
        accessing the platform, or using the service, you agree to these terms. If you are using
        Taxline on behalf of an organization, you confirm you have authority to bind that
        organization, and "you" refers to it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">The service</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        Taxline provides agentic tax operations: a fleet of specialized agents triages, extracts,
        researches, and assembles tax work into reviewer-ready output, with a confidence score and a
        citation on each field.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        <span class="font-medium text-fg">Outputs require human review and are not tax, legal, or
        accounting advice.</span> The fleet is not autonomous: a qualified person must review and
        approve work before it ships. You remain responsible for your filings, positions, and
        submissions to any tax authority.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Accounts and eligibility</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        You must be at least 18 and able to form a binding contract to use Taxline. You are
        responsible for the accuracy of your account information, for safeguarding your credentials,
        and for all activity that occurs under your account. Notify us promptly of any unauthorized
        use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        You agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-fg-muted">
        <li>Upload data you lack the rights or consent to process.</li>
        <li>Use the service to break the law or infringe others' rights.</li>
        <li>Attempt to access, disrupt, or reverse engineer the platform or its infrastructure.</li>
        <li>Resell or expose the service to third parties except as your plan permits.</li>
        <li>Submit malware or interfere with other customers' use of the service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Plans and fees</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        Taxline is offered across Personal and Business plans. Pricing below is representative and
        billed per plan; current pricing and limits are shown at checkout or in your order.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-fg-muted">
        <li><span class="font-medium text-fg">Personal — Core.</span> For solo operators getting started.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-fg">Personal — Pro.</span> For solo operators with higher volume.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-fg">Business — Team Plus.</span> For small teams sharing a workspace.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-fg">Business — Team Pro.</span> For firms with greater volume and controls.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-fg">Business — Enterprise.</span> Custom terms, security review, and support.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        Fees are billed in advance on the plan's cycle and are non-refundable except where required
        by law. We may change pricing on renewal with notice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        Taxline, including the platform, the fleet, and its software and design, is owned by us and
        protected by intellectual-property laws. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable right to use the service under these terms. You may not copy, modify, or
        create derivative works from the platform except as expressly allowed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Your data and confidentiality</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        You retain ownership of the documents and data you submit. You grant us the rights needed to
        process that data to provide the service. We do not train models on your client data. Our
        handling of personal information is described in the
        <a href={u('privacy')} class="text-accent underline decoration-accent-line underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover">Privacy Policy</a>.
        Each party will protect the other's confidential information and use it only as needed to
        perform under these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">AI disclaimer</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        Taxline produces output using AI agents. <span class="font-medium text-fg">Outputs may
        contain errors, and you must review every output before relying on it or submitting it.</span>
        We make no guarantee of accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular tax position.
        Confidence scores and citations are aids to review, not assurances of correctness. The
        service is not a substitute for a licensed tax, legal, or accounting professional.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Taxline and its suppliers are not liable for
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits,
        revenue, data, or goodwill. Our total liability arising out of or relating to the service is
        limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the event giving rise to the
        claim. The service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind
        except as required by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Indemnification</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        You agree to indemnify and hold Taxline harmless from claims, losses, and expenses arising
        from your use of the service, your data, your filings, or your breach of these terms or
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Termination</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        You may stop using Taxline and close your account at any time. We may suspend or terminate
        access if you breach these terms, fail to pay, or use the service in a way that creates risk
        for us or others. On termination, your right to use the service ends; you may request export
        or deletion of your data as described in the Privacy Policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Governing law</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, USA, without regard to its
        conflict-of-laws rules. The courts located in Delaware will have exclusive jurisdiction over
        disputes arising from these terms or the service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        We may update these terms as the service evolves or the law changes. When we make material
        changes, we will update the date above and, where appropriate, notify you. Continued use of
        Taxline after an update means you accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
        Questions about these terms? Email us at
        <a href="mailto:legal@taxline.example" class="text-accent underline decoration-accent-line underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover">legal@taxline.example</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
